{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2b3ff898-a5ec-46a3-a9c9-8a72dc44e0b1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_a107c83dbd601c73","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Qwen3.8-27B-ABLITERATED-W8A8-gdnint8/20260915T103412Z-bf20aced/runs/specialist/040d47bac9824e37a2183bd6880bda1c; date -u +%s; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\npayload = {\n \"intent_type\": \"specialist_done\",\n \"payload\": {\n  \"confidence\": 0.78,\n  \"domain\": \"serving_specialist\",\n  \"empty\": False,\n  \"gap_canonical_id\": \"gap.framework.local_explore.local_explore:0\",\n  \"new_findings\": [\n   {\"what\": \"Decode-step GPU time budget at conc=64 measured with torch.profiler on a live self-launched server (48 steps): aiter CK a8w8 GEMM 44.2% (12336 launches, 176us avg), Triton kernel_paged_attention_2d 33.8% (2165us avg x 16 steps... i.e. ~34.6ms of a ~102ms GPU-step), fused_recurrent_gated_delta_rule_packed_decode (GDN state) 13.8% (14.1ms/step), everything else <10%. The paged-attention kernel reads only ~170MB of KV per step (64 seqs x 4 kv_heads x ~1300 ctx x 24 heads x 256 hd x 2 x bf16) => ~260x off the 1.28 TB/s roofline, because its grid is (num_seqs, num_kv_heads) = 256 programs with a fully serial context-length inner loop on a 104-CU device.\",\n    \"source\": \"self-captured /tmp/prof_base trace (runs/specialist/040d.../scratch/an.py) + vllm/v1/attention/ops/chunked_prefill_paged_decode.py:461-466\",\n    \"expected_impact\": \"identifies the single fixable 1/3 of the decode step; removing it entirely would be +50%, the two available replacements measured +15-22% end-to-end\",\n    \"accuracy_risk\": \"none (analysis only)\", \"domain_tags\": [\"attention\",\"kv_cache\",\"decode\",\"roofline\",\"profiling\"]},\n   {\"what\": \"A/B on identical workloads (128 prompts x ISL1024 x OSL512 x conc64, one server per MI250X card, 2-3 repeats, all servers launched with the exact sealed base args): baseline replica 440.2/442.2/444.6 tok/s; --attention-backend TRITON_ATTN 536.6 (sequential) and 523.3 tok/s => +18 to +22%; VLLM_ROCM_SPLITKV_PA=1 + VLLM_ROCM_SPLITKV_PA_MAX_SEQS=1024 => 512.4/510.4 tok/s => +15.3/+15.4%. Greedy text spot-check identical between base and splitKV. The two levers hit the SAME bottleneck (see prior finding) via different kernels and are mutually exclusive (splitKV hooks only the ROCM_ATTN path).\",\n    \"source\": \"runs/specialist/040d.../logs/{bench,seq}_*.log + logs/srv_splitkv.log takeover lines\",\n    \"expected_impact\": \"+15 to +22% output tok/s vs the sealed baseline on this exact workload shape\",\n    \"accuracy_risk\": \"low for TRITON_ATTN (upstream standard backend, same bf16 math); low for splitKV (module ships with 576/576 float32-golden validation, greedy text matched baseline in spot check; full-corpus greedy diff was cut off by the wall clock)\",\n    \"domain_tags\": [\"attention\",\"decode\",\"env_lever\",\"config_lever\",\"gfx90a\"]},\n   {\"what\": \"The split-KV takeover gate num_seqs*num_kv_heads <= DEFAULT_MAX_SEQS=64 silently rejects this workload (64 seqs x 4 kv_heads = 256 base programs), so VLLM_ROCM_SPLITKV_PA=1 alone is a NO-OP here; VLLM_ROCM_SPLITKV_PA_MAX_SEQS must be raised too. Both env vars are unregistered in vllm/envs.py (harmless 'Unknown vLLM environment variable' warning; the module reads os.environ directly). Also: raising VLLM_ROCM_SPLITKV_PA_MAX_SCRATCH_MIB so PART_MIN stays at 64/256 measured WORSE (463.0 tok/s) than the default 32MiB budget that forces PART_MIN up to 512 for a 6272-token bound - do not 'tune' the scratch budget upward on this workload.\",\n    \"source\": \"vllm/v1/attention/ops/rocm_splitkv_pa.py:106-107,578-700 + bench_8907_r1.log vs bench_8903_r*.log\",\n    \"expected_impact\": \"makes the +15% variant actually fire; prevents the -10% scratch-budget trap\", \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"attention\",\"pitfall\",\"env_lever\"]},\n   {\"what\": \"rocm-smi's 'GPU Clock 800MHz' in the baseline summary is an idle-sample artifact: /sys/class/drm/cardN/device/pp_dpm_sclk shows the device boosts to the 1700MHz DPM level under real serving load and measured ceilings are 1264 GB/s copy BW and 125.7 TFLOPS bf16 GEMM (4096x16384x5120). sysfs is mounted ro in the container so clock locking is not available (and not needed).\",\n    \"source\": \"/sys/class/drm/card*/device/pp_dpm_sclk polled under load + scratch/bw.py, scratch/mb.py\",\n    \"expected_impact\": \"corrects the roofline denominator for future rounds\", \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"roofline\",\"hardware\"]},\n   {\"what\": \"--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16 works on this stack (overridden with a config warning), halves the GDN state page and drops the forced attention block size 784 -> 400 tokens (KV tokens 294,473 -> 328,145). Its throughput/accuracy effect was NOT measured (wall-clock cut); it interacts with both attention proposals (splitKV takeover re-validated at physical_block=400 in the server log).\",\n    \"source\": \"logs/srv_mamba.log + logs/srv_sk_mamba.log (interface.py:911, kv_cache_utils.py:1869)\",\n    \"expected_impact\": \"unknown - candidate for next round, gated on accuracy (checkpoint declares mamba_ssm_dtype=float32)\", \"accuracy_risk\": \"moderate (fp32->bf16 state storage on a W8A8 ckpt)\", \"domain_tags\": [\"gdn\",\"kv_cache\",\"memory_bandwidth\"]},\n   {\"what\": \"aiter tuned-GEMM table is a dead end here, confirming platform law 1/5 by inspection: shipped a8w8_tuned_gemm.csv contains only gfx942/gfx950 rows (0 gfx90a), so the 5747 'not found tuned config' warnings across ~1150 shapes can never match; default heuristic is the shipped behavior.\",\n    \"source\": \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/aiter/configs/a8w8_tuned_gemm.csv gfx-column census + baseline server.log\",\n    \"expected_impact\": \"negative knowledge - closes an investigation branch\", \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": 